# The record, part 5: one record, three places it shows.
columns
title "One record, three places it shows"
description "The server keeps the last thirty reads of a source. The same record shows in three places: as five marks at the end of the source's row on the status page, as a list of reads on the page of the source, and as one line in the terminal. The page of the source is drawn in the accent, because that is where the record lives in full."

column
  eyebrow "The row on the status page"
  item `docs.typo3.org`
    marks ok,ok,warn,ok,error
    boxed
  note "The last five reads, oldest first. A mark is a colour and a name, so the row reads without sight."
  foot "a glance"
column
  eyebrow "The page of the source"
  emphasis
  item `09-15 06:00  read  3m 02s` mark=ok boxed
  item `09-14 06:12  stopped  step 2` mark=error boxed
  item `09-14 00:00  read  2m 58s` mark=ok boxed
  item `09-13 18:00  slow  9m 41s` mark=warn boxed
  foot "the record in full, thirty reads"
column
  eyebrow "The terminal"
  line "$ dev-companion status docs"
  line "30 reads · 27 read · 2 slow"
  line "1 stopped · last 06:00 today"
  note "One line, for the reader who asks from a shell and never opens a page."
  foot "a sentence"
